Shiji, move!

32
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
There's a crack on the front of the brain cakes.

33
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:04,000
That armor won't take much more.

34
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
The head is damaged.

35
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Extended damage, unknown.

36
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
The controllers are breaking up.

37
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
We're not getting any readings on the pilot.

38
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
No, Shiji!

39
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:33,000
No, Shiji!

40
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,000
4.

41
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,000
1.

42
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
2.

43
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,000
2.

44
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
2.

45
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,000
3, 2, 3.

46
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
2, 1,2.

47
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,000
2, 3, 4, 5.

48
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,000
2, 3, 4, 5.

49
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:47,000
2, 4, 5.

50
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
1,2, 3, 4, 5.

51
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
1,2, 3, 4, 5, 5.

52
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
2, 3, 5.

53
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
2, 5.

54
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,000
1,2, 3, 5.

55
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Unfamiliar ceiling.

56
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:11,640
So, the angels have returned.

57
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:13,120
It's rather sudden.

58
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:16,540
It's the same as it was 15 years ago.

59
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:18,620
That's the way of disasters.

60
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:20,140
They come without warning.

61
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:26,200
On the positive side, our previous investments would appear to be not such a waste after all.

62
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,520
You can't be sure about that yet.

63
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:31,440
If it doesn't pay off, it's still a waste.

64
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:32,080
Correct.

65
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:36,020
Now that news of the angels has become common knowledge,

66
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:43,480
Nerve must take steps to control the manner in which this information is received by the general public.

67
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:47,580
You may rest assured that it's already been taken care of.

68
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:48,620
Don't worry.

69
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:54,660
Government officials have announced that in regard to the declaration of the...

70
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:55,920
This incident...

71
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,400
Oh, public scenario B-22.

72
00:04:58,860 --> 00:04:59,880
Just like we thought.

73
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:02,160
So we're covering up the truth again?

74
00:05:02,640 --> 00:05:04,720
Well, at least the PR people are happy.

75
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:06,620
They finally got something to do.

76
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,960
We're being pretty casual about it.

77
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,640
I don't think so.

78
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,960
Actually, I think we're all pretty scared.

79
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,520
Of course we are.

80
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:17,440
Well, we must acknowledge that.

81
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:23,040
But still, I wonder, Mr. Ikari, were Nerve and Ava used efficiently?

82
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:30,340
The repair costs for Unit 1 added to the development costs for Unit 0 are simply staggering.

83
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:34,860
We also understand that you gave that toy to your own son.

84
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:38,140
Time, money, and manpower.

85
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:41,800
How much more will be wasted by you and your family?

86
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:44,520
And that is not your only responsibility.

87
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,640
The Human Enhancement Project.

88
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:48,340
That should be your top priority.

89
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:49,540
Correct.

90
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:55,640
Under these desperate circumstances, that project may be the only real hope for the future of mankind.

91
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,080
Do you understand?

92
00:05:57,620 --> 00:06:02,600
In any event, the Angels are no excuse for the delay in the schedule of that project.

93
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:05,900
We may consider adjusting the budget.

94
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:08,280
The rest of the meeting does not concern you.

95
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:11,300
Your presence here was appreciated.

96
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:16,760
Ikari, you do know that there can be no turning back.

97
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:20,340
I know.

98
00:06:22,220 --> 00:06:24,600
Mankind has no time left.

99
00:06:25,640 --> 00:06:27,140
Mankind has no time left.

100
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:54,360
Man, air conditioning is the greatest thing.

101
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,240
Man, man's triumph over nature.

102
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:58,660
Shinji's finally woken up.

103
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:01,720
And how is he?

104
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:05,340
Well, his memory seems a bit muddled, but...

105
00:07:05,340 --> 00:07:07,280
You don't think it could be contamination, do you?

106
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:09,460
I don't think we should worry.

107
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:10,600
Really?

108
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:13,320
You're right.

109
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:15,440
He did have a pretty hectic day.

110
00:07:15,820 --> 00:07:16,840
Poor little kid.

111
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,460
His cerebellum must have taken a lot of stress.

112
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,020
Cerebellum?

113
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:22,320
Don't you mean his heart?

114
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:22,420
Don't you mean his heart?

115
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:23,240
Don't you mean his heart, you are Edwards.

116
00:07:23,420 --> 00:07:23,760
Right.

117
00:07:24,140 --> 00:07:28,400
It doesn't sound like he's a good friend.

118
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:48,460
He is engineers who had his Bosman.

119
00:07:48,460 --> 00:07:54,180
If Ava and this city both operated their full potential, we might make it through this.

120
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,500
You're such an optimist.

121
00:07:56,800 --> 00:08:00,860
Hey, sometimes you need a little wishful thinking just to keep on living.

122
00:08:01,380 --> 00:08:06,360
I see your point. It's nice to hear a positive attitude. I'll see you later.

123
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:08,460
Okay, see ya.

124
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:14,240
Dr. Ugae, Internal Department 1. Dr. Ugae, Internal Department 1.

125
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:18,060
Please call Dr. Azuma of the First Surgical Department immediately.

126
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:23,120
The medical conference regarding the B experiment will be held as scheduled.

127
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:26,640
All supervisors, please proceed to conference room 2.

128
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:51,220
They don't want to live together? Are you sure?

129
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:54,860
I think that living apart is natural to them.

130
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:57,600
And being together is unnatural?

131
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:02,640
He'll be living alone?

132
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:07,000
That's right. His room will be on the sixth block beyond this one. Is that all right?

133
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,300
Yes, sir.

134
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,280
Shinji? Are you sure about that?

135
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:16,960
Living alone is fine with me. I'm alone anyway.

136
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,420
What did you say?

137
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:23,640
You heard me. I said I'll be taking Shinji home to live in my place, okay?

138
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:25,760
It's already been approved.

139
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:29,740
And don't worry. I'm not going to be making any passes at him.

140
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:32,420
Of course you're not. How could you even think of such a thing?

141
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:33,660
You've got no shame at all.

142
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:35,820
Some people don't have any sense of humor.

143
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:43,900
Well, I guess we have to have a party tonight, huh?

144
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:45,180
Why is that?

145
00:09:45,180 --> 00:09:48,540
It's a welcoming party in honor of my new roommate, of course.

146
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:04,980
Are you going to move after all?

147
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,700
Yes. I'd never have dreamt that this city would become a battlefield.

148
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:08,220
Yeah.

149
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:11,420
My husband's saying that at least the kids and I should move.

150
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:15,400
Don't I know it. This city may be a fortress, but that's no guarantee of safety.

151
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,960
Just thinking about last night gives me the chills.

152
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:25,140
I hope you don't mind if we make a little stop on the way.

153
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:26,700
A stop where?

154
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:29,280
Oh, it's a really cool place.

155
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:35,060
It's so desolate.

156
00:10:36,800 --> 00:10:38,620
The city seems so lonely.

157
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:41,680
Here we go.

158
00:10:41,680 --> 00:11:08,260
Oh, it's awesome.

159
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:10,820
The buildings are growing.

160
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:27,420
This city is a fortress designed to stand against the angels.

161
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:31,320
This is Tokyo 3.

162
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,460
This is our city.

163
00:11:33,460 --> 00:11:36,040
And it's the city that you saved.

164
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:56,440
Your things ought to have been delivered already, Shinji.

165
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:58,660
I just moved here myself, you know?

166
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:02,900
Hey, come in.

167
00:12:03,660 --> 00:12:06,900
Uh, I don't want to intrude.

168
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:10,340
Shinji, this is your home now.

169
00:12:10,340 --> 00:12:20,060
I'm, I'm home.

170
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:21,820
Welcome home.

171
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:29,860
Um, as you can see, the place is just a little bit messy, but, uh, go ahead and make yourself comfortable.

172
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:32,840
Um, this is a little messy?

173
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:35,900
Oh, sorry.

174
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,920
Could you put the food in the fridge, please?

175
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,420
Uh, yes, ma'am.

176
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:40,820
Ice.

177
00:12:42,160 --> 00:12:42,640
Snacks.

178
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:46,400
And 50 gallons of beer.

179
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:49,020
What kind of life does she lead?

180
00:12:49,020 --> 00:12:57,180
Uh, excuse me.

181
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,840
What's in the other fridge?

182
00:12:58,960 --> 00:13:00,020
Oh, don't mind that.

183
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:01,460
He's probably still sleeping.

184
00:13:03,140 --> 00:13:03,700
Sleeping?

185
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:06,960
Let's eat.

186
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:09,200
Yeah, let's eat.

187
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:09,700
Oh.

188
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:14,020
Woo!

189
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:15,520
Yeah!

190
00:13:16,060 --> 00:13:17,100
Good stuff!

191
00:13:18,120 --> 00:13:21,960
You know, life just doesn't get any better than this.

192
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:23,180
Hmm?

193
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:24,620
Not hungry?

194
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:27,160
It's good, even if it is all instant.

195
00:13:28,100 --> 00:13:29,140
I'm sorry.

196
00:13:29,340 --> 00:13:32,220
I'm just not used to food like this.

197
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:32,940
What?

198
00:13:33,260 --> 00:13:34,740
Are you finicky?

199
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:35,480
Huh?

200
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,400
Um, no.

201
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:38,580
Uh, that's not what...

202
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:41,440
Oh, isn't this nice?

203
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:42,320
Uh-huh.

204
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:45,000
Having two for dinner sure beats eating alone, huh?

205
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:46,200
Uh-huh.

206
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:48,840
Here we go.

207
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:50,560
Let's go for the next one.

208
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:54,460
Paper, scissors, stone.

209
00:13:55,360 --> 00:13:58,600
Three, two, one, go.

210
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:01,660
I'm sorry, Shinji.

211
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:02,920
Okay.

212
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:06,160
That was a really fair way to split up the chores, wasn't it?

213
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:08,280
Yeah.

214
00:14:08,580 --> 00:14:11,840
This is your home, so feel free to take advantage of everything here.

215
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:14,380
Except, of course, of me, that is.

216
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:16,360
Uh, yes, ma'am.

217
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,340
Yes, yes, yes.

218
00:14:18,540 --> 00:14:19,700
Is that all you can say?

219
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:21,960
It's getting on my nerves!

220
00:14:22,060 --> 00:14:22,720
You're a boy!

221
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:23,620
Act like one!

222
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:24,740
Yes, ma'am!

223
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:25,220
Uh!

224
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:27,500
Uh, I guess that's just the way you are.

225
00:14:27,900 --> 00:14:29,180
Why don't you go take a bath?

226
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:29,960
Yeah!

227
00:14:30,400 --> 00:14:31,820
Wash away your troubles!

228
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:34,140
Bathing cleans the mind and soul.

229
00:14:34,140 --> 00:14:35,620
Uh-huh.

230
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:37,980
Ab-uh-uh-ah!

231
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:41,700
Ah!

232
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:44,200
B-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-'

233
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:44,920
Miss Misano!

234
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:45,800
What?

235
00:14:45,800 --> 00:14:46,480
What?

236
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:48,340
F�-f-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b!

237
00:14:48,340 --> 00:14:49,680
B-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b-b...

238
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:50,340
Huh?

239
00:14:51,520 --> 00:14:52,580
Oh, him?

240
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,940
He's one of those new warm-water penguins.

241
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:02,080
Uh...

242
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:04,620
Th-that was...

243
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:05,560
That was a wha-what?

244
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:06,720
His name's Penpen.

245
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,000
He's your other roommate.

246
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:10,500
Um...

247
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:12,260
Why don't you cover up?

248
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:13,680
Uh-huh.

249
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:15,120
Oh!

250
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:15,420
Oh!

251
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:21,980
Ah, I guess I should be nicer, but...

252
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:23,860
He's probably already made up his mind about me.

253
00:15:26,580 --> 00:15:28,740
Ah, Misato Katsaragi.

254
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:31,340
She's not a bad person.

255
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:33,360
Bathing clean to the mind and soul.

256
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,740
But bad memories always seem to find me in the bath.

257
00:15:38,660 --> 00:15:39,800
Like my father.

258
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:42,720
And that girl of Rei.

259
00:15:45,420 --> 00:15:48,000
So how was Rei today?

260
00:15:50,520 --> 00:15:53,240
You did see her at the hospital today, didn't you?

261
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:56,860
She can work again in 20 days.

262
00:15:57,780 --> 00:16:00,900
By then, we'll be ready to reactivate Unit Zero from cryostasis.

263
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:04,220
It's so hard on these children.

264
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,840
There's no one else who can pilot the Avas.

265
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:11,200
As long as they survive, that is what I'll have them do.

266
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:14,180
With no regard to what they may want?

267
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:38,060
Yeah, after all the horrible stuff he went through, I don't think he'll pilot again.

268
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:40,520
Maintaining him is part of your job.

269
00:16:41,540 --> 00:16:42,520
I'm just scared.

270
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:44,540
I don't know how to deal with him.

271
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:46,060
Grumbling already?

272
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:48,620
But it was your idea to take him in, you know.

273
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:49,660
Oh, shut up!

274
00:16:49,660 --> 00:16:54,760
I was just thinking of Shinji as a tool.

275
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:57,940
I'm as shameless as Ritsuko.

276
00:16:59,740 --> 00:17:01,660
We destroyed the angel, but...

277
00:17:01,660 --> 00:17:03,660
I don't feel happy.

278
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:09,120
Another unfamiliar ceiling.

279
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:12,160
Of course.

280
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:16,380
In this whole city, there's no place that's familiar.

281
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:18,820
This is your home now.

282
00:17:19,940 --> 00:17:21,460
Why am I here?

283
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:46,040
The head is damaged.

284
00:17:46,260 --> 00:17:47,400
Extended damage, unknown!

285
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:49,240
We're having problems maintaining activation.

286
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,120
Status report!

287
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:51,840
Synchrograph reversing!

288
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:52,940
The pulses are flowing backwards!

289
00:17:52,940 --> 00:17:54,100
Break the circuit now!

290
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:54,740
Do it!

291
00:17:54,840 --> 00:17:55,240
We can't!

292
00:17:55,820 --> 00:17:57,100
It's not accepting the signal!

293
00:17:57,740 --> 00:17:58,780
What about Shinji?

294
00:17:58,940 --> 00:18:00,160
His monitors aren't reacting.

295
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:01,520
His condition's unknown!

296
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:03,100
Unit 1's gone completely silent!

297
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:03,520
Misato!

298
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:05,740
We've got no choice.

299
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:06,900
Abort the operation!

300
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,560
We've got to rescue the pilot!

301
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:10,160
Eject the entry plug!

302
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:10,940
We can't!

303
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:12,280
It's completely out of control!

304
00:18:12,280 --> 00:18:13,580
What did you say?

305
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:23,380
The Ava's reactivating!

306
00:18:23,500 --> 00:18:24,400
I don't believe it!

307
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:25,640
This can't be!

308
00:18:26,500 --> 00:18:27,660
My God!

309
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:28,660
Berserker!

310
00:18:28,660 --> 00:18:50,540
We've done it!

311
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:57,680
It's an AT field!

312
00:18:58,280 --> 00:18:59,380
No, not now!

313
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:00,840
As long as that field is up!

314
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:02,320
He can't get near that angel!

315
00:19:05,260 --> 00:19:07,280
The left arm's regenerated itself!

316
00:19:07,280 --> 00:19:07,920
No way!

317
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:14,140
Unit 1's expanding its own AT field!

318
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:16,260
It's neutralizing the bay space!

319
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:19,300
No, it's breaking through it!

320
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:25,740
It went through the AT field like it wasn't there!

321
00:19:46,260 --> 00:19:57,660
It found itself destroyed!

322
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:06,540
UGER!

323
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:10,620
This guy is not destroyed!

324
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,120
E soort!

325
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:24,520
Is the Ava?

326
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:37,940
That must be Ava's true form.

327
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:47,520
Circuits reconnected.

328
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:48,520
Systems restored.

329
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:49,520
Graphs back to normal.

330
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:51,020
Pilot life science confirmed.

331
00:20:51,020 --> 00:20:53,520
Preserving the pilot's life is our first priority.

332
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:55,120
Send out the recovery team.

333
00:20:55,120 --> 00:20:56,120
Hurry!

334
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:13,120
Shindy.

335
00:21:13,120 --> 00:21:14,120
Can I come in?

336
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,120
Shindy.

337
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:17,120
Can I come in?

338
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:33,520
I forgot to tell you something.

339
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:50,620
You did something very good and very noble today.

340
00:21:50,620 --> 00:21:52,920
You should be proud.

341
00:21:52,920 --> 00:21:56,920
Good night, Shindy.

342
00:21:56,920 --> 00:22:08,920
Thank you.

343
00:22:08,920 --> 00:22:12,320
Walk me to the moon, let me playulumir stars.

344
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:16,320
Like on Jupiter and Mars

345
00:22:16,320 --> 00:22:19,320
In other words

346
00:22:19,320 --> 00:22:24,320
Hold my hand

347
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:28,320
In other words

348
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:32,320
Darling, kiss me

349
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:36,320
Fill my heart with song

350
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:40,320
And let me sing forevermore

351
00:22:40,320 --> 00:22:44,320
You are all I long for

352
00:22:44,320 --> 00:22:48,320
All I worship and adore

353
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:52,320
In other words

354
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:56,320
Please be true

355
00:22:56,320 --> 00:23:00,320
In other words

356
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:04,320
I love you

357
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:08,320
Shinji's life is busier than ever

358
00:23:08,320 --> 00:23:10,320
But he keeps to himself friendless

359
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:12,320
Until it's revealed that he's an Ava pilot

360
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:14,320
However, this new hero status brings both embarrassment

361
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:16,320
And the rap of one boy in particular

362
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:18,320
Don't miss the next episode

363
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:20,320
And I'll sneak in a little bonus, okay?

